# HeapBuddy frontend environment.
# Copy to `.env` (or `.env.local`) and adjust as needed.

# Base URL of the Go backend's JSON API.
#
# - LEAVE UNSET for same-origin relative requests ("/api/…"). This is what the
#   production single-binary build uses — the Go backend serves the SPA and the
#   API on the same origin.
# - SET to the backend origin to target a backend on a different origin. In local
#   dev the backend runs on :8080 (`cd backend && go run . serve`) while the Vite
#   dev server runs on another port; the backend reflects localhost CORS so
#   cross-origin works.
#
# Example for local dev against the backend:
# VITE_HEAPBUDDY_API_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Offline mock-data mode (no backend needed). OPT-IN: set to "true" to serve the
# bundled mock data without calling any API. Leave unset/false for real analysis.
# Note: this is a separate switch from VITE_HEAPBUDDY_API_URL — an empty base URL no
# longer implies mocks (that would make the production build show fake data).
# VITE_USE_MOCKS=true
